# tracker, etc.). Created by the harness; never load-bearing for
# the project.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Local scratch dir (TASK-0394 cycle-232): build/e2e logs, throwaway
# emit dirs, generated backend .rs, etc. Never load-bearing for the
# project. Load-bearing reason to ignore (not just declutter status):
# the three doc-citation / test-name fences that scan from the repo
# ROOT via ripgrep -- check-doc-citation-staleness,
# check-doc-citation-staleness-bare, check-doc-test-name-staleness --
# honour .gitignore. (check-mega-files / check-textual-replace-on-
# codegen / check-include-str-coverage scan explicit nucleus/.../src
# roots and never saw tmp/.) Un-ignored scratch .rs in tmp/ would be
# scanned by those three and could RED `just ci` for whoever has a
# stale file there (architect cycle-231 P3; latent today -- current
# scratch trips neither pattern). No recipe reads ./tmp/
# (the port-stress recipe uses the absolute /tmp/, not this dir).
# NB: because the fences no longer scan tmp/, a fence bite-test must
# inject into a tracked-crate path, not tmp/.
tmp/
